# Authorization boundary

Do not implement, refactor, ingest, migrate, deploy, or mutate external state unless the
current operator request authorizes that category and scope.

Research, inspection, measurement, documentation, and issue planning do not imply
runtime implementation authority. When a material design choice is missing, continue
read-only work or ask one narrow question. Do not invent scope to demonstrate activity.

Once a task is authorized, perform its safe mechanical next steps without requiring a
ceremonial “go” message. Authorization and no-onus-shift are complementary rules.
